@startuml
!theme plain

title Atomic multi-rule mutation and refresh publication

actor "OTA provisioner" as OTA
participant "Security Domain" as SD
control "ARA-M parser / catalog" as ARA
collections "inactive physical record" as Spare
database "active bitmap\nrefresh tag\nrevision" as Meta
participant "Java Card RE\ntransaction service" as JCRE

autonumber

OTA -> SD: Authenticated STORE DATA\nF0 upsert or F1 delete
SD -> ARA: Application.processData(full APDU buffer)
ARA -> ARA: Validate complete command and rule
ARA -> ARA: Find exact REF-DO / deletion matches

alt F0 is byte-identical to active rule
  ARA --> SD: 9000 (idempotent no-op)
  SD --> OTA: 9000; refresh unchanged
else Mutation changes the catalog
  opt F0 add or update
    alt ARA-M enters at transaction depth zero
      ARA -> Spare: Write length=0, rule bytes, final length\n(non-atomic; committed-state spare is unreachable)
    else Security Domain already owns a transaction
      ARA -> JCRE: Check unused commit capacity
      ARA -> Spare: Atomic copy of complete candidate record\ninside caller-owned transaction
    end
  end
  ARA -> ARA: Build next active bitmap,\nnew refresh tag, next revision in transient RAM

  critical Visibility commit
    ARA -> JCRE: beginTransaction() if callback owns none
    ARA -> Meta: Atomic copy of bitmap + refresh + revision
    ARA -> JCRE: commitTransaction() if owned
  end

  Meta --> ARA: New catalog and refresh become visible together
  ARA --> SD: 9000
  SD --> OTA: 9000
end

note over Spare,Meta
On the owned path, a torn spare write is unreachable and metadata rolls back.
On the joined path, candidate and metadata writes both roll back with the outer
transaction, even across several callbacks. After commit, only the new record
set is reachable and refresh/revision describe that same state.
end note

@enduml
